# Audio never enters git from here.
#
# Not a size rule. The repository is PUBLIC, and every candidate auditioned so
# far is free-tier Suno output, which is licensed for personal and
# non-commercial use only - pushing one would be distributing it. Git history
# also does not forget: removing a file later takes a history rewrite, not a
# delete commit, and any fork or clone keeps its copy regardless.
#
# So tracks live here locally, are fetched at runtime from static/, and are
# never committed. `npm run dev` and `npm run audio` both work on the local
# copies; a fresh clone simply has no music, which the loader handles by design
# (see music.ts - a missing bed degrades to the synthesised cue book).
#
# WHEN THE PAID-TIER TRACK ARRIVES it still has to ship inside the build, so at
# that point ONE file gets committed deliberately:
#
#     git add -f "static/music/<the chosen track>.mp3"
#
# and its ASSET_LICENCES.md row - generation URL, date, verbatim prompt, tier -
# must land in the SAME commit. Nothing else in this directory goes with it.
#
# musicTracks.test.ts enforces the other direction: every audio file present
# here must appear in ASSET_LICENCES.md, tracked or not. It skips entirely when
# the directory holds no audio, which is the normal state of a fresh clone.
*.mp3
*.wav
*.m4a
*.ogg
*.webm
